& [Purpose]
  + make current development navigation distinguish historical readiness from later proof-backed completion
  + preserve historical statements while appending machine-verifiable current supersession

& [Requirements]
  + [DSA-001] admit one strict versioned JSON inventory with exactly twenty-two entries
  + [DSA-002] each entry contains one unique repository-relative target path expected historical marker superseding status and one unique existing proof path
  + [DSA-003] target and proof paths are contained tracked non-reparse regular files with bounded nonzero bytes
  + [DSA-004] every expected historical marker remains present exactly and is never replaced
  + [DSA-005] every target appends one CurrentSupersession section naming the audit profile superseding status and exact proof path
  + [DSA-006] the inventory covers Windows sys compile probe content digest regular-file directory root inventory assembly ordered digest and ordered-digest reconciliation surfaces only
  + [DSA-007] the inventory admits no duplicate target or target-status coordinate; one completion proof may supersede multiple historical surfaces for the same feature
  + [DSA-008] an independent read-only verifier rederives target inventory tracked state physical identity markers supersession and proof conclusion
  + [DSA-009] unknown inventory fields absolute or traversing paths extra entries missing entries wrong proof paths stale markers and untracked targets refuse
  + [DSA-010] current product readiness README M2B reentry and engine navigation cite the supersession audit without deleting historical state
  + [DSA-011] verification output is one compact deterministic JSON line without absolute paths source bodies or environment state
  + [DSA-012] no Rust Cargo lock dependency package binary protocol runtime provider model service persistence effect installation delivery trust secret target selection remote FPGA or Minecraft change is permitted
  + [DSA-013] focused adversarial tests prove at least ten inventory and target refusals in a disposable copy without mutating governed files
  + [DSA-014] all PowerShell parses recursive evidence attribution commit push and post-push replay pass
  + [DSA-015] completion states only that navigation is reconciled; it grants no implementation authority to any remaining frontier

& [Delineation]
  + historical readiness is a true event record
  + current completion is a later proof-backed navigation claim
  + product maturity provider availability target selection and production authority remain separate dimensions

& [Invalidation]
  + target deletion historical marker rewrite proof-path drift duplicate entry untracked admission verifier mutation or scope expansion stops closure
